# AI-friendly architecture

## Rule

- Prefer feature-oriented vertical slices over broad horizontal layer sprawl.
- Use deep modules: small stable public APIs that hide internal complexity.

## Structure guidance

- Co-locate feature behavior: types, tests, domain logic, and interfaces close to usage.
- Keep module boundaries explicit; limit cross-feature leakage.
- Avoid god files and broad utility dumping grounds.
- Keep files reasonably small; split by responsibility when growth harms readability.

## Change strategy

- Implement in end-to-end slices for one concrete behavior at a time.
- Preserve existing architectural invariants unless explicitly changed by user direction.

## Repository invariants to preserve

- One episode equals one canonical simulation rollout.
- Train/eval/render consume the same simulation outputs.
- Simulation owns physics/camera/reward computation; render stays view-only.
- `SimulationStateSeries` remains the episode-level artifact contract.
